.\" Manual page for SLA-Slicer. Check with: groff -man -Tutf8 -ww sla-slicer.1 >/dev/null
.TH SLA-SLICER 1 "2026-11-21" "SLA-Slicer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sla-slicer \- offline slicer for SLA/MSLA resin 3D printers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sla-slicer
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B sla-slicer
.RB [ \-\-slice | \-\-export\-sla | \-\-export\-stl | \-\-export\-obj | \-\-export\-3mf ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TRANSFORM ]
.I file
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.br
.B sla-slicer \-\-sla\-run\-recipe
.I recipe.json
.RB [ \-\-input
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-report
.IR report.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SLA-Slicer
is a fork of PrusaSlicer 2.9.4 dedicated to resin (SLA/MSLA) printers.
It works fully offline: it never contacts the Internet, it does not check for updates and
it does not download profiles.
It slices 3D models (STL, OBJ, STEP, AMF, 3MF) into layer images and exports them in many
printer archive formats (for example SL1, CTB, CBDDLP/Photon, PWMX, GOO, CXDLP, UVJ, NanoDLP and Klipper MSLA).
.PP
Without an action the graphical application starts and opens the given model files.
When an action such as
.B \-\-slice
is given, the program works from the command line, without a window.
.SH OPTIONS
The list below covers the main options.
.B sla-slicer \-\-help
prints the complete list and
.B sla-slicer \-\-help\-sla
prints every SLA print configuration key, which can also be given as
.BI \-\-layer\-height= 0.05
(highest priority, above
.B \-\-load
files and values stored in 3MF files).
.SS Input
.TP
.BI \-\-load " file"
Load a configuration file; may be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-printer\-profile " name"
.TQ
.BI \-\-print\-profile " name"
.TQ
.BI \-\-material\-profile " name"
Name of the printer, print and resin material preset used for slicing.
.SS Actions
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-slice
Slice the model and export the selected SLA archive format.
.TP
.BR \-\-export\-sla ", " \-\-sla
Slice the model and export the SLA printing layers as PNG.
.TP
.B \-\-export\-stl
.TQ
.B \-\-export\-obj
.TQ
.B \-\-export\-3mf
Export the model(s) in that format.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Write information about the model to the console.
.TP
.BI \-\-save " file"
Save the resulting configuration to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-query\-printer\-models
.TQ
.B \-\-query\-print\-material\-profiles
Print the installed printer models, or the print and material presets of the selected
.BR \-\-printer\-profile ,
as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-sla\-run\-recipe " recipe.json"
Run a layer recipe: a JSON file chaining the layer operations, issue detection, exports and a conversion.
See
.B \-\-dry\-run
to check a recipe without writing anything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-sla
Show the full list of SLA print configuration options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the product version, the build id and the PrusaSlicer version this application is based on.
.SS Transform options
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Scaling factor or percentage.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale\-to\-fit " X,Y,Z"
Scale to fit the given volume.
.TP
.BI \-\-rotate " N"
.TQ
.BI \-\-rotate\-x " N"
.TQ
.BI \-\-rotate\-y " N"
Rotation angle in degrees around the Z, X or Y axis.
.TP
.BI \-\-center " X,Y"
.TQ
.BI \-\-align\-xy " X,Y"
Center the print around, or align the model to, the given point.
.TP
.BI \-\-cut " N"
Cut the model at the given Z.
.TP
.BI \-\-duplicate " N"
.TQ
.BI \-\-duplicate\-grid " X,Y"
Multiply copies by a factor, or into a grid.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-merge
Arrange the supplied models on one plate and merge them into a single model.
.TP
.B \-\-dont\-arrange
Keep the original XY coordinates of the models.
.TP
.B \-\-split
Split unconnected parts into separate objects.
.TP
.B \-\-ensure\-on\-bed
Lift the object above the bed when it is partially below (default; use
.B \-\-no\-ensure\-on\-bed
to disable).
.SS Other options
.TP
.BI \-\-datadir " dir"
Load and store settings in the given directory instead of
.IR ~/.config/SLA\-Slicer .
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
The file where the output is written (by default derived from the input file).
.TP
.BI \-\-sla\-archive\-format " id"
Output archive format for
.BR \-\-slice .
.TP
.B \-\-sla\-accept\-adjustments
When the output format cannot store a setting exactly, write the nearest storable value instead of refusing.
Every adjusted value is printed.
.TP
.B \-\-sla\-accept\-conversion
When the output format uses fewer grayscale levels than the sliced layers, export a converted copy instead of refusing.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-\-sla\-run\-recipe :
check every step and write nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " file"
.TQ
.BI \-\-report " file"
With
.BR \-\-sla\-run\-recipe :
replace the
.B open
path of the recipe; write the JSON report to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-loglevel " N"
Logging sensitivity, 0 (fatal) to 5 (trace).
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Maximum number of threads used for slicing.
.TP
.B \-\-single\-instance
Send the command line to an already running window instead of starting a second one.
.TP
.B \-\-opengl\-compatibility
.TQ
.BI \-\-opengl\-version " ABCD"
.TQ
.B \-\-opengl\-aa
.TQ
.B \-\-opengl\-debug
OpenGL selection and debugging options of the graphical application.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error (for a recipe: a recipe or step error; nothing was written).
.TP
.B 130
A recipe run was cancelled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/SLA\-Slicer/
Settings, printer, print and material presets (the
.I SLA\-Slicer.ini
file and one directory per preset kind).
On first start the SLA part of an existing
.I ~/.config/PrusaSlicer
directory is copied here; the old directory is never changed.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/SLA\-Slicer/
Used instead of
.I ~/.config/SLA\-Slicer
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG, LC_ALL
The user interface is available in English and Polish; any other locale falls back to English.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home page and documentation:
.UR https://github.com/pieotr/Sla-SlicerOS
.UE
.PP
Layer recipes (JSON automation): doc/AUTOMATION.md in the source tree.
